  "reason": "The current best (config_042: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250) strongly indicates that scvi_n200 and imagenet_vit_l are the optimal encoders, and weighted fusion is preferred. The only untested variation within this top-performing encoder pair is the aggregation method. Config_046 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) tests whether a simpler avgpool aggregation could match or exceed transformer aggregation with the best encoders. This is the most logical near-neighbor experiment to the current best, reducing uncertainty about whether transformer's advantage is intrinsic or whether avgpool might generalize slightly better. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, confirming or refuting the aggregation choice around the best-known configuration is the highest-value use of the budget, as all other untested configs involve weaker encoders (scgpt, pca_n2000), singleprofile, or image-only settings that are unlikely to surpass 0.725."
}

